  "title": "UN report attributes Red Fort blast to Al-Qaeda in Indian Subcontinent",
  "summary": "The UN Security Council report attributes the 2025 Red Fort terror attack in New Delhi to Al-Qaeda in the Indian Subcontinent (AQIS), which has expanded beyond Pakistan to include Bangladesh. The report highlights AQIS' evolution from a fragmented group to a regional terrorist entity.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The 2025 Red Fort terror attack in New Delhi was officially attributed to Al-Qaeda in the Indian Subcontinent (AQIS) according to a UN Security Council report.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "AQIS established logistics and financial networks, working in decentralized small, scattered cells instead of large units.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The attack killed 15 people and injured many more, highlighting AQIS' threat.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
